rf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them. In 2026 so far, May to June sat at 51% of normal on the middle of the grids, and June to July came back at 131%. June to July is the wettest pair at 9.28 inches, and January to February the driest at 1.81 inches. Grid 28354 shows a preliminary 129.0 for August to September 2026, an estimate from NOAA rain.</p>"}
